  "evaluation": "Responses C and B correctly identify that this is an apparent conflict under outcome_measure. First, Study A rates perceived depression as one item on a broad psychological symptom checklist, whereas Study B uses full depression scales (which the rules explicitly identify as an apparent conflict under outcome_measure). Second, Study B's extracted claim tests a treatment-by-baseline-CRP interaction rather than a main treatment effect. Response C is best because it identifies both of these outcome discrepancies and accurately includes comparator in also_differs (placebo vs placebo plus treatment as usual). Response B is a close second. Response A is incorrect because the rules state that a combination product that includes vitamin D is a normal pair, and assuming TRI 360TM lacks vitamin D simply because its ingredients aren't listed in the summary field is an overreach for an evidence map of vitamin D studies.",
  "ranking": ["C", "B", "A"]
}
